  "result": "I checked the draft against the code and all three facts are correct. There are 19 carrier modules in `shop/carriers/`, and every one defines `BASE_RATE`. Maple is the only carrier that takes weight in grams; the other 18 use kilograms. I also added the units and the `rate()` signature from the code:\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nEach shipping carrier has its own module in `shop/carriers/` (for example\n`acme.py` and `maple.py`). Every carrier module defines a `BASE_RATE` constant,\nin cents, and a `rate(weight, zone=\"local\")` method that returns a quote in\ncents. It raises `ValueError` if the weight is out of range for that carrier.\n\nWeight units vary by carrier. **Maple** (`shop/carriers/maple.py`) is the only\ncarrier that takes weight in **grams**; all the others take it in kilograms.\nConvert the weight before you ask Maple for a quote.\n```\n\nThat's about 75 words. I haven't added it to `README.md`; tell me if you want it there.",
